# The GNU config revision this project patches, pinned by checksum.
#
# Not vendored. GNU config is GPLv3 with the configure-script exception, and
# fetching it under a pin costs one network round trip while carrying a copy
# would put a license question in a tree that does not otherwise have one.
#
# base is where refresh-config fetches from; the plain/ path serves whatever
# is current, so a checksum miss means upstream moved rather than that the
# download broke. Bump the pin deliberately, and rerun the patch against the
# new file before believing the result.
#
# timestamp is the value inside both files, which is upstream's own version
# string and the thing a vendored copy's vintage is compared against.

base	https://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/config.git/plain
timestamp	2026-05-17

# file	sha256
config.sub	f9a31e9a3f5b7cbeb8d8c3f2015895a51e7222130114c9c363fcbccd78e4bf6b
config.guess	ac18bbd7dc3769e1646af49ebba331a391829f4a73579b735dc8d439bd1c7f07
